60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"The ward office presents three paths: a permanent enclosure, a rotating location, or managed collection hours. Which keeps our doors open?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Kenji"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Kenji: The ward office presents three paths: a permanent enclosure, a rotating location, or managed collection hours. Which keeps our doors open?""}]}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Kenji, I fear the enclosure brings the smell, and the rotation brings the paperwork. Perhaps the managed hours let us keep our peace?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Shizue, managed hours mean waking before seven forty. The filing rules make rotation impractical. The enclosure is the only stable option.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, stable is not the same as fair. The measurements show the current spot is physically impossible for some. I cannot support a permanent enclosure that locks in that inequality.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right that fairness matters. @Asuka, the hours are tight, but a rotation means constant change. Let us weigh the cost of peace against the cost of movement.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, the enclosure is stable, but the minutes show it breeds resentment. @Rin, the rotation is fair, but the paperwork is heavy. Which burden can we share?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I worry the rotation is too much trouble for us all. The managed hours seem gentlest, if we can manage the early wake-up.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, gentle is not sustainable. The residents’ meeting showed nobody volunteers to enforce the window. I cannot support a plan that relies on our goodwill failing.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, the residents’ meeting proves managed hours fail because people won’t enforce them. The rotation is the only option that actually shares the burden fairly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, the rotation shares the burden, but the filing clerk says every move needs its own notice. Is that practical, or just more paperwork?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Servas, the paperwork is a one-time administrative task, not a daily drain. The hours option is a daily drain on our sleep.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right. The daily drain is heavier than the one-time task. Let us choose the rotation, for it is the only path that truly shares the weight.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas, I agree. The rotation is the only way we keep our doors open. I vote for the rotating location.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Kenji, I am relieved. A fair rotation means no one suffers alone. I vote for the rotating location.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Kenji, I concede. The rotation is the only option that does not break us. I vote for the rotating location.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I am glad we found a path that is truly fair. I vote for the rotating location.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, I am glad we found a path that is truly fair. I vote for the rotating location.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
